pseudo-Boolean proof version 2.0
* Regression test (wrong verdict), version 2 spelling of the same defect: under
* `strengthening_to_core on` a `red` without an explicit subproof stored its constraint in the
* DERIVED set, where no later `red` generates a proofgoal for it. Two contradictory witnesses
* then refuted a satisfiable formula (x1 alone satisfies it).
f 1
strengthening_to_core on
red 1 y1 >= 1 ; y1 -> 1
red 1 ~y1 >= 1 ; y1 -> 0
u >= 1 ;
output NONE
conclusion UNSAT
end pseudo-Boolean proof
